# Pipeline outputs (large, reproducible)
# NOTE: these ignore directory *contents* (`results/*`), not the directory itself
# (`results/`). Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so
# the `!` lines below only work against the `/*` form.
results/*
# ...except the retrieved input sequences: 50 small FASTAs (~58 KB total) that are
# expensive to re-fetch from NCBI, gate every downstream rule, and are the thing
# that has to stay in sync between the laptop and Hellbender. Tracking them means
# a clone is runnable without an rsync step (see audit/17).
!results/sequences/
resources/sequences/
resources/expression/
.snakemake/

# FoldX license (never commit)
foldx_license.txt
rotabase.txt

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
dist/
*.pyo
*.pyd

# Conda
*.conda
*.tar.bz2

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# IDE / editor metadata
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Claude Code / instruction files (keep locally, don't commit)
.claude/*
# ...except the Hellbender guardrails, which are cluster policy rather than personal
# preference and must apply to every clone. Session state and personal overrides in
# .claude/settings.local.json stay ignored by the explicit rule below.
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
.claude/settings.local.json
# CLAUDE.md is now tracked and is being unified into one scoped file across the
# laptop and the cluster -- see PROJECT_STATUS.md before editing the laptop copy.
CLAUDE.md.bak
COPILOT.md
AGENTS.md
*.claude-instructions
*-claude-*.txt
*-copilot-*.txt

